    "Clubs and Societies – Hokkaido University\nSkip to content\nRegular Meet-up Events\nVarious social and cultural events to provide opportunities to meet and interact with people are organized. Some of the regular events organized by the Student Support Division include:\nLanguage Corner\n– Approximately once a week\nParticipants will be paired, and have a discussion in Japanese or English. Approximately 15 students usually participate in this event. It is a good opportunity to improve speaking skill in Japanese and English.\nSawakai (chat over tea)\n– Once a month approximately\nA cross-cultural gathering held once a month to provide a space where Japanese and International students can mingle with each other.\nStudent Clubs\nThere are approximately 50 cultural clubs and approximately 70 athletic clubs at Hokkaido University. If you wish to know Japan and get better acquainted with Japanese students, participation in club activities will prove to be extremely rewarding. If you want to join a club, ask the club directly.\nBelow is a list of clubs officially recognized by the University:\nCultural\nAnimation Laboratory\nWalking Club\nRPG Study\nIgo Club (Board game)\nCinema Club\nEnglish Speaking Society\nElectone Club\nCafe Project\nMale\nChorus Club\nKaruta (playing cards) Club\nMixed Chorus Club\nMagic Club\nQuiz Club\nBible Study Club\nLight Music Club\nDrama Club\nOrchestra\nLegal System Study Club\nTHE Settlement (Volunteer Group)\nTea Ceremony Club\nNature Conservation Club\nNature Club\nPhotography Club\nJazz Club\nShuma Club (fossil searching)\nShogi (Japanese Chess) Club\nBotany Club\nShodo (Calligraphy) Club\n“The Mainstreet” Newspaper Club\nDetective Story Club\nChinese Dance Club “HANA”\nCircolo Mandolinistico “Aurora” Mandolin Club\nDesign Club “+Dtips”\nRailway Train Club\nAstronomy Club\nNijino Tsudoi (LGBTQ+ Community)\nOrgan Club\nPiano Club\nBIG BAND Hokkyoku\nOil Painting Art Club\nFolk Song Club\nBluegrass Club\nLiterature Club\nJapanese Musical Instrument Club\nHU Farm Club\nMicrocomputer Club\nJapanese Folk Song Club\nStudy of Wild Birds Club\nYouth Hostel Club\n“EN” Yosakoi Soran Club\nJapanese Comedy (Rakugo)\nRecorder Ensemble\nWind Orchestra Club\nAthletic\nAikido\nAikido (Takeda Ryu Nakamura Ha)\nAmerican Football Club\nULTIMATE CLUB PADDY Club\nArt of Drawing Swords Club\nBrass Band Cheerleading Club\nOuendan Cheering Squad\nOrienteering Club\nCanoe Club\nKarate Club\nCurling Club\nArchery Club (Kyu-do)\nCompetition Dancing Club\nKendo Club\nAviation Club\nGolf Club\nCycling Club\nSoccer Club\nMountain Climbing Club\nRace Cycling Club\nAutomobile Club\nJudo Club\nShorinji-Kempo Club (Martial Arts)\nSwimming Club “Shirokuma-Kai”\nSquash Club\nModel Skiing Club\nSkiing Club (Beginners)\nSkiing Race Club\nAlpine Skiing Club\nIce Hockey Club\nFigure Skating Club\nSports Chanbara Club\nSumo Club\nRowing\nClub\nGymnastics Club\nTaido Club\nExploring Club\nWomen’s Cheerleading\nTennis Club\nSoftball Tennis Club\nTriathlon Club\nTaekwondo Club\nHorse Riding Club\nEquestrian Club\nMen’s Basketball Club\nWomen’s Basketball Club\nBadminton Club\nMen’s Volleyball Club\nWomen’s Volleyball Club\nHandball Club\nFencing Club\nBoxing Club\nField Hockey Club\nFutsal Club “Esperanza”\nBobsleigh・Luge・Skeleton Club\nBaseball Club (hardball)\nBaseball Club (semi-hardball)\nBaseball Club (softball)\nSoftball Club\nArchery Club\nSailing Club\nRiders Club HORIZON\nRifle Club\nMen’s Lacrosse Club\nWomen’s Lacrosse Club\nRugby Club\nTrack and Field Club\nHiking Club\nUpdated on\nMay 8, 2025\nShare\nFacebook\nX\nLinkedin\nBluesky\nThreads\nHokkaido University\nKita 8, Nishi 5, Kita-ku,\nSapporo, Hokkaido,\n060-0808 Japan\n+81-11-716-2111\nContact Us\nSapporo Campus Map\nHakodate Campus Map\nJobs\nGive\nSite Policy\nPrivacy Policy\nCodes of Conduct\nThe Japan Association of National Universities\nScroll to top"
